{
  "fixtureVersion": 1,
  "id": "read-update-sequence-idempotent-retry",
  "description": "A sequence whose client disconnected after admission, so its response was lost. A concurrent identical retry meets the first member in flight: that member and its dependent fail transiently and claim nothing, while an unrelated third member runs. After the delay the sequence is retried byte-identically, then with a new member in front, then with all three members: every retained disposition is returned without re-execution — the allocated identities and revisions never change — positioned by the present member's operationIndex and operationName. A second pair shows that a carrier's admission claims are one linearizable step: two identical sequences whose members depend on each other through state rather than through @name are presented concurrently, the second observes every claim of the first and is refused member by member, and, presented again after the first completes, replays both retained dispositions. Conditions are narrated, not observed. Illustrative wire example; not evidence.",
